  "version": "6.0",
  "description": "NORA intent taxonomy for T-Mobile business care contacts. L2 = TM Forum eTOM process area applied to a service family; L4 = the specific customer need. Rules are regular expressions on normalised text (lower case, apostrophes removed, digits replaced by 'num'). Tier 1 = specific evidence, 2 = moderate, 3 = domain-level fallback and care transfers, 4 = ticket follow-ups and rep-assisted contacts (they lose to any stated topic), 5 = generic request words, 6 = last resort. The earliest, most specific match wins.",
  "naming_convention": {
    "case": "UPPER_SNAKE_CASE, English, no abbreviations except industry terms (SIM, ESIM, IMEI, SMS, RCS, LAN, IP, IOT)",
    "l2": "eTOM level-2/3 process name (or its business object) + the service family it applies to, e.g. Service Problem Management + mobile voice -> MOBILE_VOICE_SERVICE_PROBLEM",
    "l4": "<OBJECT>_<CONDITION or ACTION>, e.g. INCOMING_CALL_FAILURE, NUMBER_PORT_OUT, ESIM_ACTIVATION",
    "process_ids": "eTOM IDs are quoted from Frameworx 13.0 (1.1.1.x customer, 1.1.2.x service); current eTOM renumbers these as 1.3.x (customer) and 1.4.x (service), e.g. 1.1.1.12 -> 1.3.11, 1.1.2.3 -> 1.4.6"
  },
